helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	hy	\<variable id=\"ms_doctypes\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/ms_doctypes.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\"\>Changing the Association of Microsoft Office Document Types\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	hy	To change the association of Microsoft Office file name extensions to open the files either in $[officename] or in Microsoft Office, using Microsoft Windows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314147				0	hy	In Windows Explorer, right-click a file of the type that you want to assign to another application.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_doctypes.xhp	0	help	par_id0815200803314268				0	hy	In the context menu, choose "Open with..."				20200411 15:09:53
