helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	hy	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	hy	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153711				0	hy	\<image id=\"img_id3149018\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectbeziermode.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149018\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	hy	To view the data points and control points of a curved line, select the line, and then click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the Drawing bar. The data points are represented by squares and the control points by circles. A control point might overlay a data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145587				0	hy	To adjust a curved line segment:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	51			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	hy	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	hy	Drag a data point to resize the line. If a control point overlies the data point, drag the control point until you can see the data point, and then drag the data point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	hy	Drag a control point. The curve pulls in the direction that you drag the control point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150431				0	hy	To split a curved line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	hy	You can only split a curved line that has three or more data points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3151392	59			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149941	60			0	hy	Select a data point, and then click the \<emph\>Split Curve \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150655				0	hy	To create a closed shape:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150743	62			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153080	63			0	hy	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Close Bézier\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145162				0	hy	To convert a data point on a curved line:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	64			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	hy	Click the data point you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	hy	To convert the data point to a smooth point, click the \<emph\>Smooth Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145299				0	hy	To convert the data point to a symmetrical point, click the \<emph\>Symmetric Transition\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145348				0	hy	To convert the data point to a corner point, click the \<emph\>Corner Point\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150471				0	hy	To add a data point:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373	69			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156256	70			0	hy	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Insert Points\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	hy	Click the line where you want to add the point, and drag a short distance.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154643				0	hy	If a data point does not have a control point, select the data point, and then click the \<emph\>Convert to Curve\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151186				0	hy	To delete a data point:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153624	74			0	hy	Select a curved line, and then click the \<emph\>Points \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150261				0	hy	Click the point you want to delete.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3143230	76			0	hy	On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> Bar, click the\<emph\> Delete Points\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
