helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	hy	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	hy	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965				0	hy	To convert text into a drawing object:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963				0	hy	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	hy	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395				0	hy	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	hy	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336				0	hy	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154702				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Impress\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	hy	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\"\>Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	hy	You can use the keyboard to access $[officename] Impress commands as well as to navigate through the workspace. $[officename] Impress uses the same shortcut keys as $[officename] Draw to create \<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"drawing objects\"\>drawing objects\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149602				0	hy	Selecting placeholders				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	hy	$[officename] Impress \<emph\>AutoLayouts\</emph\> use placeholders for slide titles, text, and objects. To select a placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. To move to the next placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	hy	If you press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> after you reach the last placeholder in a slide, a new slide is inserted after the current slide. The new slide uses the same layout as the current slide.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157871				0	hy	During a Slide Show				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	hy	To start a slide show, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F2\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149354				0	hy	Advance to the next slide or to the next animation effect				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	hy	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153035				0	hy	Advance to the next slide without playing object animation effects				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155263				0	hy	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageDown\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154558				0	hy	Return to previous slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	hy	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageUp\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	hy	Go to a specific slide				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	hy	Type the page number of the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150337				0	hy	Slide Sorter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153732	21			0	hy	When you first switch to Slide Sorter, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to change the keyboard focus to the workspace. Otherwise, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the workspace, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882				0	hy	Selecting and deselecting slides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155930				0	hy	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to select, and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>. To add to the selection, use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide(s) that you want to add, and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\> again. To deselect a slide, navigate to the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248				0	hy	Copying a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	hy	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to copy, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+C\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148769				0	hy	Move to the slide where you want to paste the copied slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148388	25			0	hy	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155367				0	hy	Moving a slide:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155987				0	hy	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to move, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+X\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	hy	Navigate to the slide where you want to move the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3083282	29			0	hy	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145253				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>presentations;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>timings; rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide changes;rehearse timings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recording;display times for slides\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145253				0	hy	\<variable id=\"rehearse_timings\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\" name=\"Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\"\>Rehearse Timings of Slide Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446	1			0	hy	$[officename] assists you in defining the right rehearse timings for automatic slide changes. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	hy	Prepare the slides, start the show using a special icon, tell your imaginary audience what you want to tell for the first slide, then advance to the next slide and so on. $[officename] records the display time for each slide, so the next time you play the show with automatic slide changes, the timing will be as recorded.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	hy	To record a show with rehearse timings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3149874				0	hy	Open a presentation, and switch to \<emph\>Slide Sorter\</emph\> View.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150651	6			0	hy	Start the show with the \<emph\>Rehearse Timings\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156396\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_rehearsetimings.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156396\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Slide View bar. You see the first slide, and a timer in the bottom corner.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	hy	When it's time to advance to the next slide, click the timer. To keep the default setting for this slide, click the slide, but not the timer. Continue for all slides in your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	hy	$[officename] has recorded the display time for each slide. Save your presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3145248				0	hy	If you want the whole presentation to auto-repeat, open the menu \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\rehearse_timings.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Slide Show Settings\"\>Slide Show Settings\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
