helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150101				0	hy	\<variable id=\"numbering_lines\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/numbering_lines.xhp\" name=\"Adding Line Numbers\"\>Adding Line Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	hy	$[officename] can insert line numbers in an entire document or to selected paragraphs in your document. Line numbers are included when you print your document. You can specify the line numbering interval, the starting line number, and whether to count blank lines or lines in frames. You can also add a separator between line numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	hy	Line numbers are not available in HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153410				0	hy	To Add Line Numbers to an Entire Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	hy	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>, and then select the options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3145101				0	hy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156241				0	hy	To Add Line Numbers to Specific Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3156264				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Line Numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153385				0	hy	Select \<emph\>Show numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	hy	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	hy	Right-click the "Default" paragraph style and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150222				0	hy	All paragraph styles are based on the "Default" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	hy	Click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150956				0	hy	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line Numbering\</item\> area, clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	hy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151077				0	hy	Select the paragraph(s) where you want to add the line numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3151096				0	hy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	hy	Select \<emph\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153758				0	hy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3146864				0	hy	You can also create a paragraph style that includes line numbering, and apply it to the paragraphs that you want to add line numbers to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146880				0	hy	To Specify the Starting Line Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	hy	Click in a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3150721				0	hy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	hy	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Include this paragraph in line numbering\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3148414				0	hy	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Restart at the paragraph\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153779				0	hy	Enter a line number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Start with\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153804				0	hy	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153934				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06180000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Line Numbering\"\>Tools - Line Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id3153960				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030800.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Numbering\"\>Format - Paragraph - Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\numbering_lines.xhp	0	help	par_id2212591				0	hy	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Setting_up_a_Style_for_Numbering_Lines_in_Code_Listings\"\>Wiki page about numbering paragraphs by styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Changing the Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155913				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>default templates;defining/resetting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>templates; default templates\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;default templates\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155913				0	hy	\<variable id=\"template_default\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/template_default.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Default Template\"\>Changing the Default Template\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145569				0	hy	The default template contains the default formatting information for new text documents. If you want, you can create a new template and use it as the default template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id6414990				0	hy	To Create a Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149838				0	hy	Create a document and the content and formatting styles that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156101				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	hy	In the \<emph\>New Template\</emph\> box, type a name for the new template.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	hy	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Categories\</item\> list, select "My Templates", and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	hy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149952				0	hy	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Templates\</item\> list, double-click the "My Templates" folder.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970				0	hy	Right-click the template that you created, and choose \<emph\>Set as Default Template\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149867				0	hy	To Reset the Default Template				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	hy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"File - Templates - Organize\"\>\<emph\>File - Templates - Organize\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	hy	Right-click a text file in any of the two lists, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Reset Default Template - Text Document\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\template_default.xhp	0	help	par_id3156245				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147406				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; complex formulas in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating;formulas/mean values\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147406				0	hy	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\"\>Calculating Complex Formulas in Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	hy	You can use predefined functions in a formula, and then insert the result of the calculation into a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152901				0	hy	For example, to calculate the mean value of three numbers, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145078				0	hy	Click in the document where you want to insert the formula, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	hy	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula\</item\> icon, and choose "Mean" from the Statistical Functions list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	hy	Type the three numbers, separated by vertical slashes (|).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149481				0	hy	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>. The result is inserted as a field into the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149823				0	hy	To edit the formula, double-click the field in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
