helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Inserting Cross-References				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145087				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>references; inserting cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting and updating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>objects; cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>OLE objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>draw objects;cross-referencing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;cross-references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145087				0	hy	\<variable id=\"references\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/references.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Cross-References\"\>Inserting Cross-References\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3159263				0	hy	Cross-references allow you to jump to specific text passages and objects in a single document. A cross-reference consists of a target and a reference that are inserted as \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"fields\"\>fields\</link\> in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155860				0	hy	Objects with captions and bookmarks can be used as targets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149833				0	hy	Cross-Referencing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	hy	Before you can insert a cross-reference, you must first specify the targets in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	hy	To Insert a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	hy	Select the text that you want to use as a target for the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153125				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	hy	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list, select “Set Reference”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	hy	Type a name for the target in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box. The selected text is displayed in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	hy	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>. The name of the target is added to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Selection\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	hy	Leave the dialog open and proceed to the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153370				0	hy	To Create a Cross-Reference to a Target				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7032074				0	hy	Position the cursor in the text where you want to insert a cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7796868				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\> to open the dialog, if it is not open already.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153392				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select "Insert Reference".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the target that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3154856				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format for the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the target text, and "Page" inserts the page number where the target is located. For footnotes the footnote number is inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149980				0	hy	Cross-Referencing an Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3149992				0	hy	You can cross-reference most objects in your document, such as graphics, drawing objects, OLE objects, and tables, so long as they have a caption. To add a caption to an object, select the object, and then choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Caption\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	hy	Click in the document where you want to insert the cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Cross-reference\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150236				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, select the caption category of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> list, select the caption number of the object that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150968				0	hy	In the \<emph\>Insert reference to\</emph\> list, select the format of the cross-reference. The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090002.xhp\" name=\"format\"\>format\</link\> specifies the type of information that is displayed as the cross-reference. For example, "Reference" inserts the caption category and caption text of the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3151092				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Close\</emph\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151115				0	hy	Updating Cross-References				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id3153594				0	hy	To manually update the cross-references in a document, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\references.xhp	0	help	par_id7321390				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>View - Fields\</emph\> to switch between viewing the reference names and the reference contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Moving and Copying Text in Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>sections;moving and copying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>moving; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pasting;cut/copied text sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mouse;moving and copying text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919				0	hy	\<variable id=\"dragdroptext\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/dragdroptext.xhp\" name=\"Moving and Copying Text in Documents\"\>Moving and Copying Text in Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	hy	Select the text that you want to move or copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3155606				0	hy	Do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154236				0	hy	To move the selected text, drag the text to a different location in the document and release. While you drag, the mouse pointer changes to include a gray box.\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3153148\" src=\"res/helpimg/movedata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153148\"\>Mouse cursor moving data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\dragdroptext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154257	14			0	hy	To copy the selected text, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you drag. The mouse pointer changes to include a plus sign (+).\<br/\>\<image id=\"img_id3152868\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"0.3335in\" height=\"0.3335in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152868\"\>Mouse cursor copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Hiding Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables;for hiding text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	hy	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	hy	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	hy	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	hy	To Create a Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	hy	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	hy	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	hy	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	hy	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	hy	Enter a value for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	hy	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	hy	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	hy	To Hide Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	hy	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	hy	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	hy	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	hy	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	hy	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	hy	To Hide a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	hy	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	hy	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	hy	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	hy	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	hy	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675				0	hy	To Hide a Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	hy	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	hy	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	hy	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\>, and then enter an expression in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	hy	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
