helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081C				0	hy	Click the \<emph\>Promote Level \</emph\>\<image id=\"img_id5564488\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20172.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5564488\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or \<emph\>Demote Level \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3159363\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20173.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159363\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155525				0	hy	To Change the Number of Heading Levels That Are Displayed				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\arrange_chapters.xhp	0	help	par_id3151352	79			0	hy	Click the \<emph\>Heading Levels Shown \</emph\>icon \<image id=\"img_id3151310\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20236.png\" width=\"0.564cm\" height=\"0.564cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3151310\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>, and then select a number from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Inserting a Scanned Image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156017				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;scanned images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; scanning\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scanning pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156017				0	hy	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_scan\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_scan.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Scanned Image\"\>Inserting a Scanned Image\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	hy	To insert a scanned image, the scanner must be connected to your system and the scanner software drivers must be installed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182	3			0	hy	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>The scanner must support the TWAIN standard. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>The scanner must support the SANE standard.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155915				0	hy	Click in the document where you want to insert the scanned image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	hy	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Picture - Scan\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Picture - Scan\</emph\>\</link\>, and choose the scanning source from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_scan.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	hy	Follow the scanning instructions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Conditional Text for Page Counts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108				0	hy	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228				0	hy	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257				0	hy	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	hy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	hy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166				0	hy	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256				0	hy	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page > 1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145280				0	hy	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Pages\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Then\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145305				0	hy	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Else\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Turning Off AutoCorrect 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154250				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text;turning off automatic correction\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase;changing to lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters after periods\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>quotation marks;changing automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;automatic replacement on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>underlining;quick\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders; automatic drawing on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic changes on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changes;automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;turning off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147812				0	hy	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Off AutoFormat and AutoCorrect\"\>Turning Off AutoCorrect\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147833	2			0	hy	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	hy	To quickly undo an automatic correction or completion, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	hy	To turn off most AutoCorrect features, remove the check mark from the menu \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect - While Typing\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147251				0	hy	To Remove a Word from the AutoCorrect List				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147274				0	hy	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145596				0	hy	Click the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145620				0	hy	In the \<emph\>AutoCorrect\</emph\> list, select the word pair that you want to remove.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145645				0	hy	Click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
