helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	hy	\<variable id=\"seitetext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:PageDialog\"\>Specify the formatting styles and the layout for the current page style, including page margins, headers and footers, and the page background.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154505				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Field Names\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Fieldnames\"\>Switches the field display between field names and field contents.\</ahelp\> A check mark indicates that the field names are displayed, and no check mark indicates that field contents are displayed. Some field contents cannot be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149287	4			0	hy	To change the default field display to field names instead of the field contents, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>, and then select the\<emph\> Field codes \</emph\>checkbox in the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	hy	When you print a document with \<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\> enabled, you are prompted to include the field names in the print out.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\03090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145579				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Fields\"\>Insert - Fields\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Apply				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	bm_id5028839				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>automatic heading formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	bm_id				0	hy	\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;headings\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>headings;automatic\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>separator lines;AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155962				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05150200.xhp\" name=\"Apply\"\>Apply\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149871	2			0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:AutoFormatApply\"\>Automatically formats the file according to the options that you set under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>            \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	hy	When you apply automatic formats, the following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155625				0	hy	AutoCorrect for Headings				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	hy	A paragraph is formatted as a heading when the following conditions are met:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	hy	paragraph begins with a capital letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148386				0	hy	paragraph does not end with a punctuation mark				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150564				0	hy	empty paragraph above and below the paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149030				0	hy	AutoCorrect for Bullets / Numbering				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	hy	To create a bulleted list, type a hyphen (-), star (*), or plus sign (+), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150763	18			0	hy	To create a numbered list, type a number followed by a period (.), followed by a space or tab at the beginning of a paragraph. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147507				0	hy	Automatic numbering is only applied to paragraphs formatted with the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\>, \<emph\>Text body\</emph\> or \<emph\>Text body indent\</emph\> paragraph styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941				0	hy	AutoCorrect for Separator Lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154105				0	hy	If you type three or more hyphens (---), underscores (___) or equal signs (===) on line and then press Enter, the paragraph is replaced by a horizontal line as wide as the page. The line is actually the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"lower border\"\>lower border\</link\> of the preceding paragraph. The following rules apply:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153530				0	hy	Three hyphens (-) yield a single line (0.05 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	hy	Three underscore (_) yield a single line (1 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05150200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	hy	Three equal signs (=) yield a double line (1.10 pt thick, gap 0.75 mm).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120211.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hy	Index				20200411 15:09:53
