helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153716				0	hy	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090005.xhp\" name=\"Variables\"\>Variables\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	hy	Variable fields let you add dynamic content to your document. For example, you can use a variable to reset the page numbering.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149759				0	hy	User-defined fields are only available in the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243625				0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the available field types. To add a field to your document, click a field type, click a field in the \<emph\>Select \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150703				0	hy	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154096				0	hy	Description				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149803				0	hy	Set Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150996				0	hy	Defines a variable and its value. You can change the value of a variable by clicking in front of the variable field, and then choosing \<emph\>Edit - Field\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154571				0	hy	Show Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3153669	9			0	hy	Inserts the current value of the variable that you click in the \<emph\>Selection \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147531				0	hy	DDE field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149684				0	hy	Inserts a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\> link into the document, that you can update as often as you want through the assigned name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3159196				0	hy	Insert Formula				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151322				0	hy	Inserts a fixed number, or the result of a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149494				0	hy	Input field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154829				0	hy	Inserts a new value for a variable or a User Field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149098				0	hy	The value of a variable in an Input field is only valid from where the field is inserted and onwards. To change the value of the variable later in the document, insert another Input field of the same name, but with a different value. However, the value of a User Field is changed globally.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151255				0	hy	The variables are displayed in the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> field. When you click the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> button, the dialog\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090100.xhp\" name=\"Input Field\"\>\<emph\>Input Field\</emph\>\</link\> appears, where you can enter the new value or additional text as a remark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3149034				0	hy	Number range				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3152772				0	hy	Inserts automatic numbering for tables, graphics, or text frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3147073				0	hy	Set page variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	hy	Inserts a reference point in the document, after which the page count restarts. Select "on" to enable the reference point, and "off" to disable it. You can also enter an offset to start the page count at a different number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3156267				0	hy	Show Page Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588				0	hy	Displays the number of pages from the "Set page variable" reference point to this field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3145779				0	hy	User Field				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id3151377				0	hy	Inserts a custom global variable. You can use the User Field to define a variable for a condition statement. When you change a User Field, all instances of the variable in the document are updated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090005.xhp	0	help	par_id0903200802243892				0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click the format that you want to apply to the selected field, or click "Additional formats" to define a custom format.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
