helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143276				0	hy	Tab stop (T)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3149490	16			0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_TAB\"\>Inserts a tab stop. To add leader dots to the tab stop, select a character in the \<emph\>Fill character box\</emph\>. To change the position of the tab stop, enter a value in the \<emph\>Tab stop position \</emph\>box, or select the \<emph\>Align right \</emph\>check box.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151257				0	hy	Page number (#)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3148981				0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_PAGENO\"\>Inserts the page number of the entry.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147212				0	hy	 Hyperlink (LS and LE)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120221.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631	20			0	hy	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:TP_TOX_ENTRY:PB_HYPERLINK\"\>Creates a hyperlink for the part of the entry that you enclose by the opening (LS) and the closing (LE) hyperlink tags. On the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>line, click in the empty box in front of the part that you want to create a hyperlink for, and then click this button. Click in the empty box after the part that you want to hyperlink, and then click this button again. All hyperlinks must be unique. Available only for a table of contents.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
